WEBVTT

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>Do...</i>

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:08.230
<i>Not...</i>

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:08.480
<i>Fall...</i>

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.200
What's that? Why me?

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.830
That hurt.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:50.980
Ano ano donna iro ga ima desuka?

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.280
Egao no white

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.690
Namida no blue

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:56.360
Kasanete mita toki

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.700
Honjitsu seiten nari canvas ni

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.410
Milk no ice, ramune gokun

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.080
Genki ni color topping

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.130
Oi! ough gaki please

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:17.050
Minna no nigaoe contest

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.890
Yuno

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:24.270
Yoshi! Ato de ''pun'' okoranai de ne

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.060
Miyako

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.690
Hiro

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:31.400
Switch osaretara wa-ha-ha

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.770
Sae

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:37.700
Nanka ii kimochi nareba ii kanji

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.240
Kyousou da

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.030
lchihayaku ringo tabeyo

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.660
Sou ja nainda yo

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:48.330
Sou de iinda yo

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:53.250
Kudamono wa model san

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:58.090
Saa dessin shimasho ka

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:00.970
Shukudai dayo

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:06.600
Oh no, I fell asleep.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.940
It's morning already.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.980
l had such a bad dream.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.900
l wonder why?

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.570
Oh no, I forgot to turn the TV off.

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:21.370
No way, it's going to rain?!

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.700
No, I mean, it's already this late?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.210
Jeez, what am I doing?

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.210
When are you going to turn into a butterfly?

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.380
You can't be a sleepy head all
the time, Mr. Worm.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.010
July 14th

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.010
Cool and Comfy

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.520
Come to think of it,
Miya didn't come over this morning.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.560
Oh no, she's still...

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:55.110
Miya, wake up, Miya. We'll be late!

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.400
If we're late for the exam, we'll get into trouble.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.860
Hi, Yunocchi, good morning.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.450
Thank goodness.
So, you stayed up late to study?

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:14.290
Study? No, I slept in, for like twelve hours.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.920
Twelve hours?

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.470
Looks like we can still make it.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.310
This is one of those moments when you
feel glad you live so close to school.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.850
Hiro, good morning.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.110
Morning.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.480
What's up?

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.110
They're herbs.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.900
Harp?

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.660
That's incredible, Hiro.
l didn't know you had a harp!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.330
Wasn't it expensive?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.450
What?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:58.710
Today's the last day of exam week.
I'll do my best.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:05.220
Did I bring all my pens?
l had to rush this morning, so...

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:13.350
This isn't an ordinary eraser.
l have to knead it first.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.360
Miya, do you have an extra eraser?

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.990
It's summer, indeed.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.790
This goes here, and that goes there.
This one's gotta be here.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:38.040
This must be a coincidence. It must be.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:43.340
This goes here, and the next one goes there,
l mean here. Then the next one...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.720
l must be doing it all wrong.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.190
It's summer, indeed.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:57.770
Okay, everyone. You may begin.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.690
Ms. Yoshinoya's art class exam.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.570
Question 1 : Identify the person in this picture.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.950
Why does an art exam ask a
Japanese history question?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.410
<i>Question 2:
Identify the person in this picture.</i>

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.370
Oda Nobunaga...

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.920
<i>Question 3:
Identify the person in this picture.</i>

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.800
What is his actual name?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.260
Moai?

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.720
It's summer, indeed.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.470
Please fill in the name of one
your favorite artists.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.180
This sounds like a survey, not a test.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.770
Question 12: Name one favorite painting.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.770
Please fill in with the title of one
of your favorite paintings.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.190
Painting... painting...

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.740
Please write the name of one
of your favorite sculptures.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.370
Sculpture... sculpture...

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:01.630
List at least three strengths of your
beloved Ms. Yoshinoya

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.300
and let the principal know.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.590
What? Fifty points?!

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.260
You're taking advantage of your position.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:15.350
It's summer, indeed.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.390
That should do it.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.150
I'm so hungry.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:30.160
I don't know why, but it's hard to resist
not drawing on the exam paper.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:36.250
I hear tons of noise that's definitely
not from marking answers.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.250
TWITCH

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.790
Twitch Twitch...

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.040
Twitch Twitch...

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.790
Twitch Twitch...

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.140
It's summer.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:58.270
Okay, that's it. This is the last
exam of the semester.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.150
Those in the back, please collect the
answer sheets and bring them up.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:07.570
By the way, the lowest score will be
posted at the entrance gate.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.860
Just to let everyone know.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.570
What?!

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:27.000
The principal chewed me out,
so I won't post the worst answer sheet.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.720
Miya, how did you do?

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.300
Not good.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.550
l couldn't focus

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:40.600
because I couldn't help thinking about
the summer break after the exam.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.140
Besides...

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.770
It's summer, isn't it?

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.110
It is.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.370
Blue sky...

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.080
Dazzling sun...

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.410
It's summer! Go, go, melanin!

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.290
I'm gonna bake myself!

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.380
Oh, did you come over to enjoy the sun too?

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.390
How about baking together?

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.150
Miya, are you home?

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.110
Coming!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.690
Yes?

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.570
Were you on the roof, Miya?

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.990
Yup.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:40.200
Hey, be careful. I don't want you to fall.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.330
l know.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.830
So, you were getting a suntan.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.630
In summer, you've gotta turn your skin
darker, or you'll look unhealthy.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.510
Miya, you have something on your belly.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:57.680
Huh? Miya, that's cute.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.310
Anyhow, it's hot, isn't it?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.650
It is hot.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:11.650
It's summer, so it should be hot,
and I like it, but...

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.320
l wonder if there's something
that can cool us off?

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.870
Like a chilling fright?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.370
A flight?

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:27.670
Well, the top must be pretty cool,
but I think I would give up on the way.

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:29.380
Are you talking about a fright?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.130
Yeah, a flight.

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:32.760
ls it really a fright?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:34.670
It is a flight.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.590
So, it's a fright!

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:38.510
Yes, it's a flight!

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.390
It's hot.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:47.520
l... am... an... alien...

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:53.570
Underground life-form...

00:09:53.820 --> 00:10:00.820
Preservative-free and organic carrots...

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:02.030
Sae?

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.960
Are you all right, Sae?

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.500
l also do that often.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:19.510
Jeez, what's with you guys?
Coming in without even knocking!

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.300
I'm very sorry.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:27.180
It's hot today, and we thought the first
floor might be cooler than upstairs.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:36.070
The exam is over, and we thought it'd
be more fun if you were around.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.240
Wow, hot.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:48.540
Well, Hiro seemed busy because she wanted
to work on her project at her place.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.960
As for me, I don't have any
plans for today, so...

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:55.550
Miyako, what are you doing?

00:10:55.960 --> 00:11:00.340
Oh, I'm just messing around,
looking for something interesting.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:01.930
Oh, what's this?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.550
Let's see...

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:08.060
"I love you, Kazumi. "

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:14.440
Suddenly, Shun sprang to his feet and
yelled at the setting sun.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.480
Five hours after the scheduled time,

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:21.360
standing in the rain without an umbrella,
Yusaku was still waiting for Kyoko.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:25.120
She couldn't understand his naïve side.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.910
Oh, Sae...

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.750
No!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.500
Jeez, it's even hotter because of you.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.880
The pool! I want to go to the swimming pool.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:43.800
Why don't we go to the swimming pool?

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.850
Pool, pool, pool...
The swimming pool?

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.430
Pool, pool, pool...

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.730
l can't go, so please ask someone else.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.350
Huh? Why not?

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:58.940
Well, this is embarrassing.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.240
I'm actually a saw.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:09.540
It's a totally wrong metaphor,
but I get that you can't swim.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:19.760
l know. Wait here, Sae. I'll go get the pool.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.300
Go get the pool?

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.680
Ta-da!

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.260
That's awesome.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:33.600
A vinyl pool? Well, I kinda guessed
it right, but why do you have it?

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:37.810
When I decided I'd be living alone,
my parents gave it to me.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:40.480
Nice parents, huh?

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:43.280
Do you need it for living alone?

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:46.910
This way, I can even rent a
room without a bathtub.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.490
What kind of parents are they?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:53.120
You've got no problem using it,
right, Yunocchi?

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.790
l think I'll be all right.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:01.090
You think? There's no way you
could drown in this pool.

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:04.260
By the way, Miyako, do you
have a bathing suit?

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.390
l have the school one.

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.930
That's like going to use the pool at school.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:11.640
What about you, Yuno?

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.020
l have one I bought last year.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.350
Okay, I think I have...

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:23.610
Miyako, you can use these,
a t-shirt and bikini bottom.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.240
Oh, thanks.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:30.910
Sae, why wasn't it a bikini set?

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.080
Did you lose the top?

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.660
No, not that.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:39.290
l didn't want her to complain that
the top would be too tight.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:43.960
Umm...

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.340
Umm...

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:49.090
Umm, oh yes. You are slender, Sae.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.140
Yeah, maybe.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.650
Do you like it here?

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:08.610
That's right. You can use the
yard any time. I'm envious.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.120
Yeah, that's the privilege of
living on the first floor.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.240
Go ahead and put the air in, Yuno.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.910
What?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:16.910
You can't?

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:20.080
All right, I'll do my best.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.800
l wonder if I can finish it by the evening?

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:34.970
No, Yuno, you're supposed to use that.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.770
ls that a...

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:40.350
What? You've never used a pump?

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:48.240
l used to have a vinyl pool, but I was
small so my dad did it for me.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.740
Come to think of it, we don't
usually use it, do we?

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.660
You only need it when you
want to inflate stuff

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:56.660
like a vinyl pool or a vinyl boat
or an air mattress.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:00.580
Floats and beach balls can be inflated by
blowing air into it, and that's quicker.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.210
Okay, I'll do it then.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:08.220
l might not look it, but I'm an
expert in using a pump.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:12.390
l wish I could include it in my special
abilities on my resume.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.390
Pump: Class-3

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.390
<i>Admitted</i>

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:21.100
Yuno, let's go change.
It's all yours, Miyako.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.020
Okay.

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:29.820
The pump sends air in.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:33.820
You can send me some cookies,
but I might be in trouble.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:37.700
But I'll be happy anyway.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.340
Let me ask. What the hell are you doing, Hiro?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.640
Testing your endurance?

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:58.350
It's hot. I thought you were
working on your project.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:03.350
Yes, I was working on the project to
slim down my body for the summer.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.480
ls that what you meant by working?

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.780
That aside, why are you guys dressed like that?

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:13.780
We were wading in the vinyl pool Miya brought.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:18.490
It was fun, so we wanted
you to join us, but...

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.910
Okay, let's jump in!

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.660
Boy, nabe stew is the best in summer.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:03.870
No one says that. Besides, how can you
eat that much in this heat?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.420
But haven't you got a sudden
craving for nabe?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.750
It's great because you get to eat a lot of
veggies and it's totally healthy.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.170
What kind of nabe do you like?

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.380
l like the salty chanko-nabe.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.550
l like sukiyaki.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:19.510
l like a vegetable nabe.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.140
l love kimchi nabe.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:23.980
To help you lose weight?

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.770
The best part of nabe is to be
able to eat with a group.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.730
Hey, don't just keep eating meat.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.570
Here comes the Magistrate of Nabe.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:38.570
Come to think, what's the connection
between magistrate and nabe?

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:43.370
There are many other bossy titles.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:47.120
No one says Chairman of Nabe.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:49.790
l said, stop eating only the meat.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:54.210
Miya, Chairman of Nabe sounds like the
company president of a nabe seller.

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.510
No Nabe Police or Nabe Elder.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:02.390
No Nabe President or Nabe
Prime Minister either.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.180
Didn't you hear me?
Stop eating only the meat!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.020
Nabe clinician...

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:11.400
Nabe charismatic hair stylist...

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:14.780
Nabe best model in jeans...

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.070
Are you listening?

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.540
It's hot!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.500
What the hell are we doing?

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:44.560
Come to think, it's so hot today, so I could have
lost weight by just exercising normally.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:48.100
It's cold and feels so good.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:19:01.910
Looking into the sky makes me feel like I'm
floating in the sea. Don't you think so?

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:05.120
Yeah, I do, like in the Bering Sea.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.330
Why the Bering Sea?

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:14.840
There are more suitable vacation spots,
the like Caribbean Sea or Aegean Sea.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.960
l haven't been to the beach in a while.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:22.180
I'm more like a swimming pool person,

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:26.100
because it's scary not to be
able to stand on my feet.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.270
I'm a saw after all.

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:29.850
A saw?

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.480
Yup, grind, grind, grind...

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:37.190
l wonder why the ramen noodles you eat
by the ocean taste awfully good?

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.190
Curry rice, too.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.950
Enough of stories about food.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:48.410
Oh, I know this came out of nowhere,
but I had a strange dream this morning.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:49.700
A dream?

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:54.290
Yes, I was chased by someone in a red cloak.

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.130
That's weird.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:20:00.090
But a dream signifies the deep psyche
of the person, doesn't it?

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:06.680
Oh, I got it. Yunocchi doesn't want to
be chased by a guy in a red cloak.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.560
l said, ''signifies.''

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.440
Hey, is that a thunder cloud?

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.190
Looks like it.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:20.650
Every time I see it, it reminds me that it's...

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:23.070
Summer!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.490
Miya, what're your plans for
the summer break?

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:33.160
Me? I'll go to the beach.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.670
I'm envious. I can't go because I'm a saw.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.960
What do you mean by ''saw?''

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.840
Yup, she's a saw.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:51.100
It's evening just before the night.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.890
Summer Ocean

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.310
I'm so glad I'm done with all the exams.

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:01.990
l don't think I'll get a red card
by failing any subjects.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:05.530
Wait, what I kept seeing was... a red curtain?!

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.950
A red curtain...

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.030
Did it mean a red card?!

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.620
How did I know?

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:23.510
Oh my God, oh my God, Mr. Worm!
My Mr. Worm!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.300
What the?

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:26.890
Wow!

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:49.620
A moth!

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.660
That larva was for a moth?!

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.120
It's rather gross.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.120
It flew!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.460
Don't come this way!

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.000
Oh, it escaped through the window.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.960
It entered your room, Hiro.

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:05.630
No!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.800
End of July 14th

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:08.680
<i>To Be Continued</i>

